From fb2139b2141d3a9cf3b9686ca7ddb469ce2d52a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gauravgpai <gauravgpai300@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:34:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add a Hi3516CV610/CV608 (cv6xx) backend

The cv6xx SoCs use HiSilicon SDK V5, which renames the V4 region API msposd
already drives on hi3516ev300 to ss_mpi_rgn_* with ot_* types. The new target
builds the GOKE render path (one ARGB1555 overlay on VENC channel 0) and only
swaps the SDK calls in bmp/region.c. VENC overlay alpha runs to 255 on V5.

sdk/hi3516cv6xx/include holds the nine headers ss_mpi_region.h pulls in, from
openhisilicon b0d848e.

Built with the OpenIPC musl toolchain and linked against the
hisilicon-osdrv-hi3516cv6xx libraries; not yet run on hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
